    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="chat-todo-agent" class="doc-h2">3b. In-chat Todo-create job (code now; runner later)</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">This is <strong>code</strong> in <code>Model::AI2::TodoCreate</code>, called at the start of <code>AI2::Chat::process</code>. It is not a spawned LLM agent and it does not skip AISYSTEM W2 (the AGENTS runner). Chat-with-AI is the first caller; other agents should call the same Perl job later.</p>
            <p class="doc-body">Tracking: <a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2217" class="doc-link" title="Opens todo #2217 — the work item that tracks this Todo-create agent (write a todo from chat, not navigate to a form).">todo #2217</a> on <a href="[% c.uri_for('/project/details') %]?project_id=280" class="doc-link" title="Opens project #280 AISYSTEM, the project todo #2217 is attached to.">#280 AISYSTEM</a>.</p>
            <table class="doc-table">
                <tr>
                    <th class="doc-th">Step (agent settings)</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">Job</th>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">Parse</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Read intent. Ask only for missing subject or project. Infer priority/due/scheduled_date (queue eligibility). Do NOT invent blockers or a queue-aware start_date here — that is the Scheduler agent (<a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2218" class="doc-link" title="Opens todo #2218: Scheduler agent for blockers and start dates that respect the existing queue.">#2218</a>). LOOKUP/READ_DOCS may refine later.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td">LOOKUP_TODOS (sub-agent)</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Similar open todos on this SiteName — do not duplicate.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">LOOKUP_PROJECTS (sub-agent)</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Match project/sub-project on current SiteName. If none, ask to create a project.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td">READ_DOCS (sub-agent)</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Skim /Documentation for the topic so the todo is grounded in what the app already has.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">WRITE</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Create the row in code (TodoCreate), not by asking the chat model to invent a form. If the request is unclear, a cheap already-warm model may extract subject/project JSON only.</td>
                </tr>
            </table>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><strong>Trigger:</strong> user says “add/create a todo …” in the widget, <code>/ai/widget</code>, or the editor chat.</li>
                <li><strong>Model:</strong> none for a clear “add a todo …” (fastest, $0 — no LLM). The dropdown model must not own the write. If phrasing is unclear, extract subject/project with a <em>free already-warm</em> OpenRouter model (Nemotron nano is fine for that — no Ollama cold load). Use local Ollama only if it is already resident. The model returns JSON; <code>TodoCreate</code> writes the row. Nemotron’s failure was inventing a fake Add box, not being too dumb to parse a title.</li>
                <li><strong>Job:</strong> SiteName of the current site → match project/sub-project → ask to create a project if none fit → write a todo with <code>project_id</code>, <code>scheduled_date</code> (today), developer = logged-in user, so it shows in planning.</li>
                <li><strong>Code:</strong> <code>Model::AI2::TodoCreate</code> + intercept at the start of <code>AI2::Chat::process</code> (the path <code>/ai2/chat</code> always takes). Shared JS: <code>ai-chat/feature-todo.js</code>.</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="doc-success">
                <p class="doc-body"><strong>Built (2026-08-20):</strong> clear “add a todo …” never reaches the picker model. Parse infers scheduled_date / NEW / priority / due; asks only if subject is vague or no project matches; WRITE uses current SiteName. <code>/ai/widget</code> loads <code>feature-todo.js</code>.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="doc-warning">
                <p class="doc-body"><strong>Not built:</strong> LOOKUP_TODOS / READ_DOCS as separate callable agents; Nemotron-JSON extract for messy phrasing; other agents calling this job via the W2 runner; blockers and queue-aware start_date (that is <a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2218" class="doc-link" title="Scheduler agent tracking todo.">#2218</a>).</p>
            </div>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="scheduler-agent" class="doc-h2">3c. Scheduler agent (specified — not built)</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">This is <strong>not</strong> Parse and not bulk Reschedule. Tracking: <a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2218" class="doc-link" title="Opens todo #2218 on project #280 — Scheduler agent that creates predecessor blocker todos and sets start_date after the current queue, without rewriting every todo.">todo #2218</a> on <a href="[% c.uri_for('/project/details') %]?project_id=280" class="doc-link" title="Project #280 AISYSTEM, the project this scheduler work is attached to.">#280 AISYSTEM</a>.</p>
            <p class="doc-body">Today, creating a todo does <em>not</em> create its blockers. If the work cannot start until an inventory item exists, that inventory-create work should be a <strong>blocking predecessor</strong> (<code>is_blocking</code> / <code>blocked_by_todo_id</code>). Start dates also ignore the queue: if open work may take a month, the new todo should not start today. The old <code>/todo/reschedule</code> path rewrote <code>start_date</code>/<code>time_of_day</code> on every row and produced noise — do not revive that.</p>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><strong>Job:</strong> one agent that only makes schedule order: propose (then write, after compare) blocker chains and capacity-aware start dates.</li>
                <li><strong>Callers:</strong> Todo-create after WRITE; Daily Plan; later the AGENTS runner. Cross-plan: scoring lives in planning (#138 / TodoRanking); this agent uses it, does not replace it.</li>
                <li><strong>Safety:</strong> advisory preview first (same lesson as FocusTune weights). Never bulk-mutate the queue.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="chat-invoice" class="doc-h2">3d. Invoice from chat (draft only — shipped 2026-08-26)</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">Code in <code>Model::AI2::InvoiceCreate</code>, same intercept as TodoCreate. Tracking: <a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2311" class="doc-link">#2311</a> on <a href="[% c.uri_for('/project/details') %]?project_id=121" class="doc-link">#121 AIC-004</a>. Reuses existing Inventory tables — no new schema. Chat never Posts the GL.</p>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><strong>Trigger:</strong> “enter/record this invoice from &lt;supplier&gt; for $X …” or “create a sales invoice for &lt;name&gt; for $X”.</li>
                <li><strong>Write:</strong> supplier bill → draft on <code>inventory_supplier_invoices</code> (<a href="[% c.uri_for('/Inventory/invoice') %]" class="doc-link">/Inventory/invoice</a>). Sales → draft on <code>inventory_customer_invoices</code> (<a href="[% c.uri_for('/Inventory/sales') %]" class="doc-link">/Inventory/sales</a>). SiteName of the page. Admin or accounting role. Missing amount or unknown supplier: ask.</li>
                <li><strong>Not built:</strong> auto-create supplier; Post GL from chat; line-item SKU matching.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="shipped-0826" class="doc-h2">3e. Shipped 2026-08-26 (aisystem worktree — not committed)</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">Branch <code>aisystem</code>. Do not treat schema-branch table creation as in scope. User reviews diffs before commit.</p>
            <table class="doc-table">
                <tr>
                    <th class="doc-th">Item</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">Tracking</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">Code / gate</th>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">SuperGrok first; never OpenRouter Grok</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2313" class="doc-link">#2313</a></td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><code>Router::_detect_provider</code> remaps <code>grok-*</code> and <code>openrouter|x-ai/grok-*</code> to SuperGrok. Default is SuperGrok <code>grok-4.6</code> when OAuth exists. Fail → OpenRouter <code>:free</code> (no grok slug) then Ollama. Tests in <code>t/model_ai2_router_outage.t</code>.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td">OpenRouter 503 retry + clean errors</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2292" class="doc-link">#2292</a> / <a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2293" class="doc-link">#2293</a></td>
                    <td class="doc-td">502/503/504 retry twice (1s, 2s) then hop-down. Widget never shows raw <code>OpenRouter provider error: 503</code>. Fallback keeps the same system prompt / ACTION contract.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">Invoice from chat</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2311" class="doc-link">#2311</a></td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><code>InvoiceCreate</code> + <code>/ai2/action create_invoice</code>. Draft only. <code>t/model_ai2_invoice_create.t</code>.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td">Positive learning (partial)</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><a href="[% c.uri_for('/project/details') %]?project_id=288" class="doc-link">#288 AILEARN</a> <a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2299" class="doc-link">#2299</a></td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><code>KnowledgeRecall</code> injects prior docs/todos into the system prompt with UNVERIFIED/INTERNAL labels. It currently reads the DB <code>documentation</code> table, which is empty — live KB is file-based <code>root/Documentation</code>. Next: point recall at the file store. No new table on this branch (schema later).</td>
                </tr>
            </table>
            <p class="doc-warning">Next AISYSTEM-specified work after this: Scheduler <a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2218" class="doc-link">#2218</a>, or W1 AIMPS shortlists <a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2194" class="doc-link">#2194</a>. Do not start schema <code>AiKnowledge</code> from aisystem.</p>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="hermes" class="doc-h2">4. Hermes focus settings (W0 — applied 2026-08-19)</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">Settings live in <code>~/.hermes/config.yaml</code> via <code>hermes config set</code> (never hand-edit). Secrets stay in <code>~/.hermes/.env</code>.</p>
            <p class="doc-info">2026-09-25: SuperGrok weekly % is <strong>not</strong> an xAI API. grok.com Settings → Usage is scraped in-tab by add-on <code>grokcom-usage@comserv.local</code> (Downloads copy for Snap file picker). Writes <code>root/static/ai/grokcom_usage.json</code>. Guard script <code>~/.hermes/scripts/supergrok_daily_guard.py</code> every 15 min (user crontab). Reset anchor <strong>2026-10-01 10:31 PDT</strong>. Cap = remaining Build % ÷ days until reset. Off → <code>openrouter/cohere/north-mini-code:free</code>. On → <code>xai-oauth/grok-build-0.1</code>. Applies to <strong>new</strong> Hermes sessions only. <code>opencode-free</code> is dead — never put it in the chain.</p>
            <table class="doc-table">
                <tr>
                    <th class="doc-th">Role</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">Alias</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">Resolved</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">When</th>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">This session (2026-09-25)</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">default</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><code>xai-oauth/grok-4.6</code></td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Does not follow the guard until a new chat</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td">Coding (budget SuperGrok)</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><code>code</code></td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><code>xai-oauth/grok-build-0.1</code></td>
                    <td class="doc-td">When the guard is ON SuperGrok</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">Daily/week cap hit</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">default</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><code>openrouter/cohere/north-mini-code:free</code></td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Spread the SuperGrok week; OpenRouter cash only if free hops fail</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td">Cheap / local</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><code>cheap</code> <code>local</code></td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Ollama <code>gemma4-64k</code> / <code>qwen2.5-coder:14b</code></td>
                    <td class="doc-td">True $0. Check live aliases; do not assume.</td>
                </tr>
            </table>
            <p class="doc-body">Also on this machine (not aliased): <code>qwen2.5:72b</code>, <code>gemma4-64k</code>, <code>phi4:14b</code>. Use 72b only when a local deep-read beats a paid call. In-session: <code>/model code</code> or <code>/model cheap</code>.</p>
            <p class="doc-body">Remaining worktree <code>.hermes.md</code> files are owned by <a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2142" class="doc-link">todo #2142</a> on GITWT-NEW — raised, not absorbed.</p>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="providers" class="doc-h2">4b. In-app providers (current)</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">The /ai and /ai2 model dropdown (and the floating Chat with AI widget) has <strong>four groups</strong>. SuperGrok is not a nickname for xAI.</p>
            <table class="doc-table">
                <tr>
                    <th class="doc-th">Group</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">Wire prefix</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">Who sees it</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">Credential (any container)</th>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">Ollama (Local)</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><code>ollama|…</code></td>
                    <td class="doc-td">All roles (local models)</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Live Ollama on the host</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td">SuperGrok (weekly subscription %)</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><code>supergrok|grok-4.6</code> first</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">admin / developer / editor only</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Lowest Grok subscription — do not add money. Meter is grok.com Settings → Usage (Build / Chat %), not x.ai and not an API. Live numbers: Firefox add-on → <code>/static/ai/grokcom_usage.json</code>. Next reset 2026-10-01 10:31 PDT. OAuth token still used for Hermes chat; it cannot read that bar.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td class="doc-td">xAI (Grok)</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><code>grok|…</code></td>
                    <td class="doc-td">admin / developer / editor only</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Pay-per-token <code>GROK_API_KEY</code> / <code>/run/secrets/grok_api_key</code> / DB service <code>grok</code></td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <td class="doc-td">OpenRouter</td>
                    <td class="doc-td"><code>openrouter|…</code></td>
                    <td class="doc-td">Role-filtered (guests: :free only)</td>
                    <td class="doc-td">OpenRouter key (k8s / env / DB)</td>
                </tr>
            </table>
            <p class="doc-warning">The same slug <code>grok-4.6</code> can appear under SuperGrok and under xAI. Pick SuperGrok (prepaid) to spend weekly credits. Router (2026-08-26): <code>grok-*</code> and <code>openrouter|x-ai/grok-*</code> are remapped to SuperGrok. App default is SuperGrok <code>grok-4.6</code> when the OAuth token exists — not paid OpenRouter. SuperGrok fail → cheaper OpenRouter <code>:free</code> (never a Grok slug) → Ollama. After send, status must stay SuperGrok if SuperGrok answered; if it fell back, the :free/Ollama hop is correct, not Grok-on-OpenRouter.</p>
            <p class="doc-body">W1.0 (<a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2202" class="doc-link">#2202</a>) delivered the four-group picker. Routing fix <a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2313" class="doc-link">#2313</a>. Remaining W1 is AIMPS shortlists/sort, not another provider.</p>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="park" class="doc-h2">5. Parked until W1 gate (do not cancel)</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">These stay in the DB at priority 9 so they stop winning the daily queue:</p>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li>AIC leftover phases #242–246 (AIC-007..011) — predates Router/AIMPS</li>
                <li>Ollama fine-tune / Modelfile OFT #266–278</li>
                <li>chain_query multi-model #262–265 — after shortlists exist</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-body">Keep live: <a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=562" class="doc-link" title="Older live todo: AI create todos.">#562</a>, <a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2217" class="doc-link" title="Todo-create job (code).">#2217</a>, <a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2218" class="doc-link" title="Scheduler agent (specified).">#2218</a>, #778 (document adding a project), GITWT Hermes context #2142–2146, AIMPS #2024–2036.</p>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="skills-search" class="doc-h2">5b. Skills &amp; web search (in progress)</h2>
            <p class="doc-body">
                Two v2 capabilities: <strong>DB-backed, approval-gated skills</strong>
                and a <strong>web search that actually works</strong>.
            </p>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><strong>Skills live in MariaDB, not JSON</strong> — a config file
                    only reaches production at the next deploy and each branch mutates
                    its own copy. Approval is mandatory: new rows default to
                    <code>pending</code> and only <code>approved</code> rows are ever
                    injected, so an AI-written skill cannot change behaviour on its own.
                    Admin approves in chat; non-admins get a todo raised.</li>
                <li><strong>Table creation is a <code>schema</code>-branch action</strong> —
                    todo <a href="[% c.uri_for('/todo/details') %]?record_id=2430" class="doc-link">#2430</a>.
                    The Result class <code>AiSkill</code> exists; an admin materialises
                    <code>ai_skills</code> via in-app schema-compare. Never hand-DDL.</li>
                <li><strong>Web search</strong> — the <code>use_search</code> flag was
                    dropped between <code>Chat.pm</code> and the provider, so the widget
                    checkbox never worked. Fixed and verified. Search is self-hosted
                    (<code>comserv2-search</code>) because OpenRouter's
                    <code>search_domain_filter</code> is silently ignored — measured:
                    a Wikipedia-only filter returned zero Wikipedia results — so scope
                    control requires a service we run.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-body">
                Full design:
                <a href="[% c.uri_for('/Documentation/AiSkillsAndWebSearch') %]" class="doc-link">/Documentation/AiSkillsAndWebSearch</a>
            </p>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="golden-data" class="doc-h2">5c. Golden Data / Anti-Hallucination (code in aisystem 2026-09-24 — not committed)</h2>
            <div class="doc-warning">
                <p class="doc-body"><strong>Honest status:</strong> the Golden Data store is <strong>EMPTY / NOT YET QUALIFIED</strong>.
                    No existing corpus is golden. The <code>ai_golden_data</code> table is <strong>pending schema-compare</strong>
                    (Result <code>AiGoldenData</code> exists; an admin creates the table in-app — never hand DDL).</p>
            </div>
            <p class="doc-body"><strong>Glossary</strong> (one canonical copy): <code>lib/Comserv/Util/AI/Glossary.pm</code>
                (+ <code>Glossary.md</code>). <em>Golden Data</em> = organization-agreed truth fed to AI models, from corporate policy,
                verified research in our databases, and verified documentation of how the app runs. A record is golden only once it is
                agreed/verified (<code>status=golden</code>); existing in the DB is not enough. <em>Candidate Data</em> = records, docs,
                notes or retrieval hits that have not passed review.</p>
            <h3 class="doc-h3">Intended golden pipeline</h3>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><strong>Sources:</strong> (1) corporate policy (<code>domain=policy</code>), (2) verified research in our DBs
                    (<code>domain=research</code>, e.g. <code>ency.ency_herb_tb</code>), (3) verified app documentation
                    (<code>domain=app_docs</code>). Also <code>todo</code>, <code>customer</code>; other domains accepted.</li>
                <li><strong>Flow:</strong> <code>candidate</code> &rarr; <code>in_review</code> &rarr; human-agreed <code>golden</code>
                    (or <code>rejected</code> / <code>stale</code>). Code only ever writes <code>candidate</code>. No auto-promotion.</li>
                <li><strong>Review-first queue</strong> (not imported yet): existing policy docs, research tables such as
                    <code>ency.ency_herb_tb</code>, and app documentation. Nothing was bulk-imported in this change.</li>
                <li><strong>source_ref convention:</strong> <code>policy:&lt;doc&gt;</code>, <code>research:ency_herb_tb:4</code>,
                    <code>app_docs:Documentation/X</code>, <code>web:searxng:&lt;url&gt;</code>.</li>
            </ul>
            <h3 class="doc-h3">Policy (enforced in code — <code>Model::AI2::Grounding</code>)</h3>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li>Factual turns retrieve first: Golden Data, then Candidate Data (store candidates, prior web hits, live SearXNG),
                    each labelled <code>[GOLDEN]</code> or <code>[CANDIDATE — unverified]</code> with id + source + retrieved_at
                    (max 6 snippets / 6000 chars).</li>
                <li>Payload: glossary + "answer ONLY from GROUNDING" + cite ids (<code>[G:12]</code>, <code>[C:web-3]</code>).
                    Post-check strips uncited factual sentences and records <code>flagged_count</code>.</li>
                <li>Nothing retrieved: no model call; the user sees exactly
                    <em>"I don't have golden data for this yet, so I can't give you a verified answer."</em></li>
                <li><strong>Web / SearXNG hits are Candidate Data</strong> — answers built only from them are prefixed
                    "Unverified — Candidate Data only".</li>
                <li><strong>Flag:</strong> <code>root/config/ai_grounding.json</code> <code>mode</code> = off | <strong>shadow (default)</strong> | enforce.
                    Shadow leaves live Chat unchanged and records grounded=0 in the Ledger. A request can opt in with
                    <code>{"grounding":"enforce"}</code> or out with <code>{"creative":1}</code> / <code>{"grounding":"off"}</code>.</li>
                <li><strong>Ledger:</strong> existing <code>ai_usage_logs</code> gains grounded, golden_hit_count, candidate_hit_count,
                    snippet_ids, flagged_count, feature (Result updated; columns pending schema-compare; mirrored in metadata.grounding meanwhile).
                    Admin monitor: <a href="[% c.uri_for('/ai/usage') %]#ledger-grounding" class="doc-link">/ai/usage</a>.</li>
                <li><strong>Tests:</strong> <code>t/ai_golden_grounding.t</code> (stubs; no DB, no model).</li>
            </ul>
            <h3 class="doc-h3">Next steps</h3>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li>Admin: create <code>ai_golden_data</code> and sync the six Ledger columns via <code>/admin/schema_compare</code>.</li>
                <li>Human review UI for the review-first queue (later). No auto-promotion, no training / fine-tuning.</li>
                <li>Decide when to switch <code>mode</code> from shadow to enforce (after reviewed golden rows exist).</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="eval-reports" class="doc-h2">5d. Daily AI Eval Reports (code in aisystem 2026-09-25 — not committed)</h2>
            <div class="doc-warning">
                <p class="doc-body"><strong>Status:</strong> the tables <code>ai_eval_report</code> and <code>ai_eval_proposal</code> are
                    <strong>pending schema-compare</strong>. Until an admin creates them, the pages say "Table not created yet — run schema compare"
                    and ingest answers <code>503 {"ok":0,"error":"table_missing"}</code>.</p>
            </div>
            <p class="doc-body">The AI usage monitor's daily report lives in the app so admins can review it, tune it, and approve changes.
                It extends the usage monitor: a summary card on <a href="[% c.uri_for('/ai/usage') %]#eval-reports" class="doc-link">/ai/usage</a>
                links to the admin-only pages <code>/ai/eval</code> (list, newest first) and <code>/ai/eval/report/&lt;id&gt;</code> (detail).
                Code: <code>Controller::AI::Eval</code>, <code>Model::AI2::EvalReports</code>, <code>Util::AI::EvalAllowList</code>,
                Results <code>AiEvalReport</code> / <code>AiEvalProposal</code>. Terms: <em>Eval Report</em>, <em>Eval Proposal</em>,
                <em>Allow-listed Config Change</em> (<code>Util/AI/Glossary.pm</code>).</p>

            <h3 class="doc-h3">Schema compare (admin, once)</h3>
            <ol class="doc-body">
                <li><code>/admin/schema_compare</code> → ency → "Result files without tables" → <code>AiEvalReport</code> → Create Table.</li>
                <li>Then <code>AiEvalProposal</code> → Create Table.</li>
                <li>Backfill: on <code>/ai/eval</code> press <strong>Import inbox</strong> (reads <code>data/ai_eval_inbox/*.json</code>;
                    the 2026-09-25 seed is there), or run <code>perl script/ai_eval_ingest.pl --inbox</code> with the token set.</li>
            </ol>

            <h3 class="doc-h3">Ingest contract</h3>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><strong>URL / method:</strong> <code>POST /ai/eval/ingest</code> (dev: <code>http://127.0.0.1:4006/ai/eval/ingest</code>). Other methods → 405.</li>
                <li><strong>Headers:</strong> <code>Content-Type: application/json</code> (else 415) and
                    <code>Authorization: Bearer &lt;token&gt;</code>. Body max 2 MB (413).</li>
                <li><strong>Token:</strong> env <code>AI_EVAL_INGEST_TOKEN</code> on the server, else the first line of
                    <code>~/.comserv/secrets/ai_eval_ingest_token</code> (outside the repo; Docker: <code>/home/comserv/.comserv/secrets/</code>).
                    Minimum 16 characters. Never hard-coded. No token configured → every Bearer / anonymous call gets
                    <code>403 {"ok":0,"error":"ingest_token_not_configured"}</code>; wrong token → <code>403 {"ok":0,"error":"forbidden"}</code>.</li>
                <li><strong>Admin session</strong> also works (browser/fetch) with header <code>X-CSRF-Token</code> = the token in the /ai/eval forms; missing → <code>403 {"error":"csrf"}</code>.</li>
                <li><strong>Upsert</strong> by (<code>report_date</code>, <code>source</code>). Re-posting updates summary / markdown / metrics, never touches
                    <code>admin_notes</code>, and never duplicates proposals (dedupe by title within the report, case- and space-insensitive).
                    New proposals are stored as <code>proposed</code>.</li>
            </ul>
<pre class="doc-code">{
  "report_date": "2026-09-25",              // required, YYYY-MM-DD
  "source": "AI usage monitor",             // optional (default), max 100
  "created_by": "AI usage monitor",         // optional
  "summary": "Bot 90% left ...",            // optional text
  "markdown": "# Daily AI Eval Report ...", // optional, max 1,000,000 chars
  "metrics": {                              // optional JSON object (or "metrics_json": "&lt;string&gt;")
    "bot":        { "percent_left": 90, "previous_percent_left": 78, "soft_allowance_pct_per_day": 29, "burn_estimate_pct_per_day": 5.6 },
    "openrouter": { "balance_usd": 19.49, "day_usd": 0.0001, "week_usd": 0.0006, "month_usd": 40.43,
                    "caps": { "day_usd": 1.65, "week_usd": 11.5, "month_usd": 50 } },
    "supergrok":  { "spoken_pct": null, "last_reset": "2026-09-24T10:31:00-07:00", "prior_cycle_used_pct": 93 },
    "hermes":     { "sessions": 18, "default_model": "grok-4.6", "dashboard_9119": "down" },
    "chat":       { "host": ":3001", "window_days": 1, "calls": 7, "usable": 1, "zero_token_ok": 3, "http_404": 2 },
    "helpdesk":   { "note": "No figures reported" }
  },
  "proposals": [                            // optional, max 50
    { "title": "Enforce grounding",         // required, max 255, dedupe key
      "change_type": "config",              // config | code | workstation | other (default other)
      "target": "ai_grounding.json:mode",   // config targets must be allow-listed to be applicable
      "rationale": "why",
      "payload": { "value": "enforce" } }   // config: {"value": ...}; others: any JSON
  ]
}</pre>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><strong>200</strong> <code>{"ok":1,"report_id":7,"created":1,"proposals_created":3,"proposals_skipped":0,"warnings":[]}</code>
                    (warnings list config proposals whose target/value is not applicable; they are stored but cannot be applied).</li>
                <li><strong>400</strong> <code>{"ok":0,"error":"bad_json"}</code> or <code>{"ok":0,"error":"validation","errors":["report_date is required (YYYY-MM-DD)"]}</code></li>
                <li><strong>403</strong> <code>ingest_token_not_configured</code> | <code>forbidden</code> | <code>csrf</code>;
                    <strong>405</strong> <code>method_not_allowed</code>; <strong>413</strong> <code>too_large</code>; <strong>415</strong> <code>unsupported_media_type</code></li>
                <li><strong>503</strong> <code>{"ok":0,"error":"table_missing","detail":"..."}</code>; <strong>500</strong> <code>{"ok":0,"error":"internal"}</code> (details in the app log).</li>
            </ul>

            <h3 class="doc-h3">Review / apply flow (review-first, like Golden Data)</h3>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><code>proposed</code> → <strong>Approve</strong> / <strong>Reject</strong> (rejected / reverted can be re-approved). All buttons are POST forms, admin-only (same check as <code>/ai/usage</code>), with a per-session CSRF token.</li>
                <li><strong>Apply</strong> shows only on <code>approved</code> + <code>change_type=config</code> + allow-listed target. It reads the current value into
                    <code>before_value</code> (<code>{"present":1,"value":...}</code>), validates the new value, writes the JSON atomically (temp file + rename, same key order,
                    2-space format), sets <code>applied</code> + <code>applied_by/at</code>, and logs to the app log and to <code>result</code>.</li>
                <li><strong>Revert</strong> (applied only) restores <code>before_value</code> exactly (removes the key if it was absent), sets <code>reverted</code>, and notes drift if the value changed since apply.</li>
                <li><code>code</code> / <code>workstation</code> / <code>other</code> are never applied. Approving creates a todo in project <code>AISYSTEM</code>
                    through <code>AI2::TodoCreate</code>'s insert path (no LLM rank hand-off) and stores <code>todo_id</code>; if it fails the reason goes into <code>result</code>.</li>
                <li>Admin notes / tuning form per report (kept across re-ingest).</li>
            </ul>

            <h3 class="doc-h3">Allow-list (<code>Util/AI/EvalAllowList.pm</code> <code>%ALLOW</code>, files in <code>root/config/</code>)</h3>
            <table class="doc-table">
                <thead><tr><th>Target</th><th>Allowed</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td><code>ai_grounding.json:mode</code></td><td>off | shadow | enforce</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>ai_grounding.json:max_snippets</code></td><td>int 1..20</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>ai_grounding.json:max_total_chars</code></td><td>int 500..20000</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>ai_grounding.json:postcheck_action</code></td><td>strip | flag</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>ai_grounding.json:web_search</code></td><td>0 | 1</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>ai_usage.json:alert_percent</code></td><td>int 1..100</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>ai_usage.json:supergrok_monthly_limit_usd</code></td><td>number 0..500</td></tr>
                    <tr><td><code>ai_usage.json:supergrok_monthly_request_limit</code></td><td>int 0..100000</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
            <p class="doc-body">Anything else is rejected. <strong>Routing:</strong> there is no router config file. Free-model preference is
                <code>@FREE_PREFERENCE</code> in <code>Util/ModelCatalog.pm</code>, the startup catalog is <code>_default_free_catalog</code> in
                <code>Model/AI2/Router.pm</code>, and <code>pick_free_fallback</code> walks the live catalog. So routing proposals are <code>code</code> and become todos.
                <strong>Caps:</strong> only <code>ai_usage.json</code> holds caps (SuperGrok USD / requests / alert %). The OpenRouter soft caps ($1.65/day, $11.50/week, $50/month)
                are not in any app config. The <code>xai_auto_fill</code> / <code>openrouter_auto_fill</code> billing flags are intentionally not allow-listed.</p>
            <p class="doc-body"><strong>Tests:</strong> <code>t/ai_eval_reports.t</code> (in-memory SQLite + temp config copies; no live DB, no real config).</p>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

